Rule 1 (input must be floating-point or complex dtype: 6–10)
{v_1 : tensor} |= 6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 3 (out dtype must match input’s result domain: real→same float dtype, complex→same complex dtype)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if 6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8 then dtype_(v_2) = dtype_(v_1) else if 9 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10 then dtype_(v_2) = dtype_(v_1) else false
>>
Rule 4 (out must have the same shape as input)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
